From cc94945d5f513d2f25b4494fad5ba3572051c7bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:45:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: size the MAC max frame length to the port's MTU

The mEMAC max frame length was programmed once at init to the FMan-wide
fsl_fm_max_frm, and the driver had no ndo_change_mtu. With
FSL_FM_MAX_FRAME_SIZE=9600 a port at MTU 1500 therefore accepted ~9.6K
frames. The MAC applies the limit to the whole frame, FCS included, and
adds no room for a VLAN tag.

Add FM_MAC_SetMaxFrameLength() (mEMAC only; the FM keeps its per-MAC
bookkeeping and the port's limit check) and fm_mac_set_max_frame_length()
in the wrapper. sdk_dpaa now sets the limit to
max(mtu, 1500) + ETH_HLEN + ETH_FCS_LEN, plus VLAN_HLEN while the port
has any upper device and twice that once a VLAN on it is 802.1ad or
carries a VLAN of its own, capped at fsl_fm_max_frm. It is applied on
registration, whose failure now fails it, on MTU change and on every
upper link/unlink of the port or of a VLAN over it.

Without the jumbo buffer layout, also cap max_mtu at what one Rx buffer
holds behind its headroom, so fsl_fm_max_frm alone cannot advertise an
MTU the buffers were not sized for.
